{
  "case_id": "2021-21-588",
  "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: General Prelogar, would you spend just a few minutes on the United States' interest that gives you a basis for being involved in this suit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: You -- you based your involvement quite a bit on Debs. Can you give me a couple of examples where the United States has taken a similar action based on Debs?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Well, actually, what I'm more interested in is, have you done something similar when a constitutional right has been involved?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: -- you'd agree that tort laws for defamation have a chilling effect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0001-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: Well, Mr. Chief Justice, the equitable remedy that we're seeking here is not limitless. It is the traditional remedy of enjoining implementation of an unconstitutional law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0001-0013",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: No, we're seeking an injunction against those who actually choose to involve themselves in the constitutional violation by filing suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0001-0016",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: Well, Justice Alito, if that's what the statute was attempting to accomplish, then, presumably, it would apply those liquidated damages to every single S.B. 8 plaintiff."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0001-0017",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: We did not try to do that. And, again, I think this relates to my answer to the Chief Justice that the injunction doesn't reach the world at large or every possible person, the anyone anywhere who is authorized under this law to bring suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0001-0019",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: That's right, Justice Sotomayor. And I think that that reflects that the relief that we're seeking is in some respects different than the relief that the providers could obtain in their suit because they don't have a mechanism to identify or sue the S.B. 8 plaintiffs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0001-0021",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: I think that it's actually every injunction operates that way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice GORSUCH: Okay. Then is this an advisory opinion saying don't file these things, we will throw them away, but we -- we have no contempt power to enforce the injunction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice GORSUCH: On -- on -- on the Debs question that the Chief Justice raised, just to press that a little bit further, an assertion of an equity right here, and I think Justice Thomas alluded to this too, has the United States Government ever before asserted this equity right to protect individual rights in any other state ever?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice GORSUCH: Besides that one suit, are you aware of any others?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General PRELOGAR: If the state structured that hypothetical law in this same way, then we would have the same concern that the state is effectively seeking to take the issue away from the courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: And one final point. The -- why wouldn't -- and -- and I think I -- you know, I've alluded to this before, I'd asked this before -- why wouldn't these private individuals be considered private attorneys generals? The -- because so much seems to be -- one thing that seems rather implicit on the other side is that they are in effect, if not in designation by law, attorneys generals because they are enforcing a statewide policy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Let me think of --of just a specific example which was the worst one I could think of for you, the -- the --I mean, suppose a governor filed this, you know, had this model law and said anyone who brings a black child to a white school is subject to, you know, and then we copy the law. Here we are. Now, if you were in that situation, which I'm sure you're glad you're not, what? What would you do? I mean, if we uphold this, are we retroactively upholding that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So can I -- MR. STONE: -- to maintain a cause of action -- JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- give you examples -- MR. STONE: -- under the equal protection clause."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I mean, if that's right, you know, and we say that, we would live in a very different world from the world we live in today. Essentially, we would be inviting states, all 50 of them, with respect to their un-preferred constitutional rights, to try to nullify the law of -- that this Court has laid down as to the content of those rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Texas",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STONE: Respectfully, Your Honor, I have to disagree with you on two points, the first one being the State of Texas hasn't nullified anything. The State of Texas specifically set up in state law a recognition of this Court's holdings in Casey, providing an undue burden defense, particularly to recognize that this Court's holdings bind state courts in their adjudication."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But it does have an obligation to follow, to respect people's federal constitutional rights?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: If some abortions have been chilled, is there any way to determine the degree to which that is the result of the potential for S.B. 8 suits from the degree to which it is attributable to the fear of liability if Roe or Casey is altered?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3e46a8bdb64a-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Do you agree, to follow up on the Chief Justice's questions, that state clerks, court clerks, and state judges enforce state law when they entertain private civil suits?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-21-588",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "3e46a8bdb64aefe3aed3ed2cc07afb471f671417e5d8ffb8077bcf4b710be9e4",
